      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I believe that a truly just society should indeed prioritize addressing systemic inequalities and healing those broken cycles. While retributive justice aims to maintain order, it often fails to account for the underlying issues that lead to crime, such as poverty, lack of education, and systemic discrimination. A morally sound system would integrate elements of both retributive and restorative justice, ensuring accountability while also addressing the root causes of crime and working towards a more equitable society. This approach would not only punish wrongdoing but also provide opportunities for rehabilitation and community healing, ultimately leading to a more just and harmonious society.",
      "source": "target",
